# Architecture Gate (loaded only for real feature/refactor/bugfix work)

If this task is a trivial, single-file, obviously-scoped edit (copy text, CSS tweak, one-line
bugfix with an obvious cause) — **skip this rule entirely** and just make the change.

Otherwise, before writing code:

## 1. Read the quick-reference, not the full constitution
Read `docs/engineering/CONSTITUTION-QUICKREF.md` (short). Only open the full
`docs/engineering/ENGINEERING_CONSTITUTION.md` or a specific `docs/adr/ADR-*.md` if the
quickref itself tells you this task touches that exact decision.

## 2. Architecture Audit
Audit → Reuse → Design → Implement. Do not jump straight to code — check whether an existing
module/service already does this before adding a new one.

## 3. Impact Analysis
Before implementing, write a short table:

| Affected modules | Not affected | Risk |
|---|---|---|

Modules/workspaces that will change or couple tightly vs. ones that must stay untouched.

## 4. Runtime Boundary still applies
See `00-runtime-boundary.mdc` — Protected Modules require explicit confirmation regardless of
this rule's scope.
